  "schema": 1,
  "notes": "Agent-harness verdicts (waired-ai/waired-agent#322): can this model actually drive a coding agent's tool-call format? Measured by internal/agentgrade against the real gateway, never asserted from reputation, generation, or context-window size — the model that started this (qwen2.5-coder-14b) advertised tool_use, shipped the standard Hermes template, and belonged to a well-regarded coder series.\n\nREAD THE RATIO, NOT THE VERDICT. `verdict` is the WORST outcome across every trial, so it is a function of the trial count: any model with a nonzero per-call failure rate converges to \"fail\" as trials grow, and a \"pass\" only means no draw went wrong. What distinguishes a model is cases[].failed / cases[].trials. Several entries here read \"fail\" on one bad trial in 24 and sit beside entries that failed 24 of 24; treating those as the same finding is the mistake this field exists to prevent.\n\nEvery entry carries the engine and version it was measured on, the fixture revision, the waired-agent commit whose GATEWAY produced the answers, the transport(s) driven, and the date — because compliance is a property of (model, quantisation, engine, harness) and not of the weights alone. Verdicts from different fixture_revision values were measured against different request weights and are NOT comparable; verdicts from different agent_revision values may have been measured before a gateway change that altered the answer (#409 moved four models from failing every tool call to passing without the fixture moving a byte; #458 then taught the gateway to retry a turn the engine could not deliver, and qwen3.5-9b went from 11 failures in 72 case-trials to 3 — the same weights, the same engine, a different answer).\n\nThe retirement worklist does not read `verdict` at all: it asks whether a case's failure rate is above catalog.RetireFailureRate at 95% confidence, which on this data selects qwen2.5-coder-0.5b and nothing else.\n\nRe-measure with: make e2e-agentgrade MODEL=\u003collama tag\u003e TRIALS=12 [STREAM=1], then `catalog-tool agentgrade --import unary.json --import stream.json` to pool both runs.",
